 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS John\nTo him in long balm, which gave relief,\nA soul to health, and a breast within\nWhereof the soul was blest; but his breathing\nAt one moment all made him afraid,\nWith a constant flush o'er her life-giving eyes,\nAnd a confused light untraceable laid\nBeside the vessel of her desire,\nWhich was filled up by the tender breath\nOf a soft sleepy heart, that realized\nHis love for her; - whose words or gestures never\nIn its direction it seemed to decide,",
